## Distributed-Erlang node name. quod does NOT cluster over Erlang distribution
## (all peering is QUIC), but relx's boot script REQUIRES a -name/-sname, and a
## host-shared EPMD means the name MUST be unique per host. Nomad sets
## QUOD_DIST_NAME=quod_<p2p-port>@<ip> (RELX_REPLACE_OS_VARS substitutes it at
## boot); the Dockerfile ENV default (quod@127.0.0.1) guarantees a valid,
## non-empty name on any plain `docker run`, so the var is never empty in
## practice. Outside the image you must export QUOD_DIST_NAME yourself.
-name ${QUOD_DIST_NAME}
-setcookie quod_dev_cookie

+K true
+A 16
+sbwt very_short
+sbwtdcpu very_short
+sbwtdio very_short

## Max-ports cap. With +Q unset the BEAM sizes its port table from the
## container's open-file limit (ulimit -n). Container runtimes default nofile
## to ~1e9, pinning the table at 2^27 slots and PREALLOCATING ~1.5 GiB of
## port_table even on a node that uses a handful of ports (the entire "2 GB"
## footprint we chased — confirmed via erlang:system_info(allocated_areas)).
## 65536 is ample (one stream per peer per namespace) and shrinks it to KB.
+Q 65536
